W: 2. May she live in mirth and jollity
W: With a fa la la la la la la
W: and past-time with good company
W: With a fa la la la la la la
W: and he who would not join in glee
W: must puritan or papist be
W: and him we curse with misery
W: With a fa la la la la la la la la laaaaaaa
W: With a fa la la la la la la
W:
W: 3. Let the Queen's good health go round and round
W: With a fa la la la la la la
W: and let her praises loud resound
W: With a fa la la la la la la
W: and he who would not have it so
W: may he be cursed with a gouty toe
W: and days of wrath and nights of woe
W: With a fa la la la la la la la la laaaaaaa
W: With a fa la la la la la la
W:
W: 4. Our goodly Queen is fair of face
W: With a fa la la la la la la
W: endowed with every female grace
W: With a fa la la la la la la
W: and every woman in this shire
W: who doth not to the like aspire
W: may her breast be dun and her hair be wire
W: With a fa la la la la la la la la laaaaaaa
W: With a fa la la la la la la
W:
W: 5. So now we've raised our tankards high
W: With a fa la la la la la la
W: We've raised them full and lowered them dry
W: With a fa la la la la la la
W: Elizabeth, long may she reign
W: may all here join in this refrain
W: and fill our tankards up again
W: With a fa la la la la la la la la laaaaaaa
W: With a fa la la la la la la
